# NEEDS THE MECHANISM BUILD (Burke-Dryer H2/O2, 13 species, from PelePhysics):
#   make POSTFIX=2d-g++-bd AMREX_TARGET=ext/AMReX-Codes/amrex/2d-g++-26.02 \
#        HYDRO2_MECH=ext/AMReX-Combustion/PelePhysics/Mechanisms/BurkeDryer bin/hydro2-2d-g++-bd
# SI units.  Gas at rest in a periodic box: T = 1200 K, p = 1 atm (rho = 0.32059 kg/m^3), mole fractions 2 : 1 : 7.
# Reference: the same mechanism (its mechanism.yaml) in a Cantera constant-volume reactor -- temperature, pressure
# and species against time, ignition delay (time of the steepest temperature rise, 7.2e-5 s).
# Checks the thermally perfect equation of state (T and p from the sensible phase energy), the production rates, the
# reactor integrator and the energy bookkeeping (rho E changes by the heat released only).
# Phase 0 is a trace (eta = 1e-6) of an inert perfect gas; phase 1 carries the mechanism species IN ITS ORDER.
#
# Run (from bin/): mpirun -np 1 ./hydro2-2d-g++-bd ../tests/FlowChemistry/input_0D_H2O2Ignition plot_file=<dir>/output
# Check:           tests/venv_cantera/bin/python ../tests/FlowChemistry/reference/h2o2_check.py ignition <dir>
